# Zig source must have LF line endings: the compiler rejects a carriage return
# outside a string literal, and `zig fmt` reports every CRLF file as needing
# reformatting. This is a Windows library, so every checkout of it is the case
# that gets this wrong by default -- git for Windows ships with
# `core.autocrlf = true`, and GitHub's windows runners inherit that.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores text normalised and checks it out that way on every
# platform. Nothing in this repository is meant to hold a carriage return.
* text=auto eol=lf
